<Legal title="Cookie Notice" heading="Cookie Notice" description="Which cookies and similar technologies swarmnest.ai uses: no advertising or tracking cookies, only strictly necessary security and payment cookies." path="/cookies/">
<p>Cookies are small files a website stores in your browser. Similar technologies include local storage and small scripts that measure page views. This notice explains which ones are involved when you use swarmnest.ai.</p>

<h2>What we use</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Type</th><td>Who and why</td><td>Needs consent?</td></tr>
<tr><th>Strictly necessary security</th><td>Cloudflare, our host, may set cookies such as <code>__cf_bm</code> or <code>cf_clearance</code> to tell people from bots and to block attacks. They do not identify you personally and expire quickly (for example, <code>__cf_bm</code> lasts about 30 minutes).</td><td>No: needed to deliver the site securely.</td></tr>
<tr><th>Payments</th><td>When you check out, Stripe's checkout pages set their own cookies for fraud prevention and to make payments work. These are set by Stripe on Stripe's pages under the <a href="https://stripe.com/legal/cookies-policy" rel="noopener">Stripe cookie policy</a>.</td><td>No: needed to complete a purchase you ask for.</td></tr>
<tr><th>Analytics</th><td>We may use Cloudflare Web Analytics, which counts page views and performance without cookies and without fingerprinting or tracking you across sites.</td><td>Cookieless; no cookies stored.</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>What we do not use</h2>
<p>Our own site code does not set cookies. We do not use advertising cookies, social media pixels, cross-site tracking or third-party analytics such as Google Analytics. That is why there is no cookie banner: we only use technologies that are strictly necessary or cookieless.</p>

<h2>Your choices</h2>
<p>You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings. Blocking Cloudflare's security cookies may mean you see more security checks; blocking Stripe's cookies may stop checkout from working.</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>If we ever add cookies that are not strictly necessary (for example, accounts, preferences or a newsletter tool that tracks clicks), we will update this notice and, where the law requires, ask for your consent first. See also our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
</Legal>
